'''Okpe''' is an [[Edoid language]] of [[Nigeria]] spoken by the [[Urhobo people]].

==Phonology==
The sound system is rather conservative, and nearly the same as that of [[Urhobo language|Urhobo]]. The vowels system is the same, and somewhat reduced compared to proto-Edoid: there are seven vowels, {{IPA|/i e ɛ a ɔ o u/}}.<ref>Archangeli & Pulleyblank, 1994. ''Grounded phonology'', p 181''ff''</ref> Of the [[consonant]]s, only significant differences are the addition of {{IPA|/ɣʷ/}} and of the distinction between ''l'' vs ''n'' and ''y'' vs ''ny'': these alternate, depending on whether the following vowel is oral or nasal. {{IPA|/ɾ, ʋ, w/}} also have nasal [[allophone]]s before nasal vowels.

